In article <1991Nov5.182138.1590@usenet.ins.cwru.edu>, ak751@cleveland.Freenet.Edu (Mark Saltzman) writes...
> Ok, I know that I need to spend a few days ftp'ing (through the mail)
> the 38 pieces of the nethack source from uunet.uu.net.  do these pieces
> comprise nethack 3.0 with no patches applied?  if so, do i need to get
> all the patchlevel files starting with 1a, up to 10h in order to build
> patchlevel 10, or can i just get 10a through 10h.

     If you start with those 38 parts, then yes, you would need every
one of those other files to get to 3.0j.  However, 3.0 patchlevel 9 was
a complete repost, in 56 parts, plus one patch for DOS termcap support.
It's in comp.sources.games/volume10/nethack3p9 (or something pretty close
to that).  Don't waste your time and effort getting 3.0 and patches 1
through 9, but get 3.0pl9 plus patch 10 (which I think ended up in
volume7/NetHack3).

> also, since i will not be building nethack on a unix system will i need
> some special program to apply the patches?

     They could be applied manually if you were really desparate, but
that would be tedious and error prone.  The Unix-style patch utility is
also available on the network.  (Not sure where though; you might try
comp.sources.misc archives at uunet.)  If you specified which non-Unix
system you're talking about, somebody might be able to give a better
answer.

